+## 2026-04-23 - status GitHub queue blind spot fixed
+- Root cause: `scripts/automation/sane-status-crossref.sh` used a hardcoded seven-app GitHub repo list, so it omitted infra/support repos like `sane-apps/SaneProcess`, `SaneUI`, `SaneAI`, `Sane-AppleDocs`, `Sane-XcodeBuildMCP`, and `homebrew-tap`. `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb status` also was not in the Mini-first routing set.
+- Fixes:
+  - `sane-status-crossref.sh` now uses org-wide `gh search issues` and `gh search prs` against `sane-apps`, groups results by repo, and includes URLs.
+  - Earlier sales/inbox/listing section failures now print a warning and continue, so GitHub issues/PRs cannot be hidden by an unrelated transient failure.
+  - `scripts/SaneMaster.rb` now Mini-routes `status`.
+  - Codex and Claude status skill docs now point SaneProcess status runs at `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb status`, not the raw shell script.
+  - `DEVELOPMENT.md` and `scripts/automation/README.md` document org-wide GitHub coverage.
+- Regression test:
+  - `scripts/automation/status_crossref_test.py` proves a SaneProcess issue and PR appear, PRs returned by issue search are filtered out, and GitHub sections still run after sales/inbox failures.
+- Verification:
+  - Local: `bash -n scripts/automation/sane-status-crossref.sh`, `python3 -m unittest scripts/automation/status_crossref_test.py`, and `ruby -c scripts/SaneMaster.rb` passed.
+  - Mini canonical: `ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb status` routed to Mini, completed end to end, and surfaced open issues `SaneBar #136`, `SaneBar #129`, `SaneProcess #8`, and `homebrew-tap #1`.
+  - The same Mini run surfaced 30 open PRs across `Sane-AppleDocs`, `Sane-XcodeBuildMCP`, `SaneClip`, `SaneProcess`, and `SaneVideo`, including `SaneProcess #9`.
+- Current status caveat: `check-inbox.sh` still has its own GitHub subsection that only shows SaneBar issues; the canonical status runner's new org-wide sections are now the source of truth for the full queue.
